// BT-3971: a Tier 2 block body ending in `[...] value` that assigns a local
// answered the raw `{Value, State}` tuple in an Erlang FFI argument block
// (a compile error now, BT-3947 parks the right answer). This pins the REPL
// host: the root evaluated block answers 3, and the FFI block that writes a
// captured local is now rejected earlier, as an ADR 0133 escaping block
// (BT-3917), before the BT-3971 error can apply.

t := 0
// => 0

[n := 3. n] value
// => 3

(Erlang lists) map: [:x | t := t + 1. [n := 3. n] value] with: #(1)
// => ERROR: `t` is assigned in a block passed to Erlang
